{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A discarding group that contains dynamically created child tasks."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiscardingTaskGroup","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To create a discarding task group,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"call the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withDiscardingTaskGroup(returning:isolation:body:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t use a task group from outside the task where you created it.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In most cases,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the Swift type system prevents a task group from escaping like that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because adding a child task to a task group is a mutating operation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and mutation operations can’t be performed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from a concurrent execution context like a child task."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Refer to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" documentation for detailed discussion of semantics shared between all task groups.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Discarding behavior","anchor":"Discarding-behavior","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A discarding task group eagerly discards and releases its child tasks as"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"soon as they complete. This allows for the efficient releasing of memory used"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"by those tasks, which are not retained for future "},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls, as would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be the case with a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Cancellation behavior","anchor":"Cancellation-behavior","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A discarding task group becomes canceled in one of the following ways:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"when ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/cancelAll()","type":"reference"},{"text":" is invoked on it,","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"when the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task","type":"reference"},{"text":" running this task group is canceled.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Since a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscardingTaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a structured concurrency primitive, cancellation is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically propagated through all of its child-tasks (and their child","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tasks)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A canceled task group can still keep adding tasks, however they will start","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"being immediately canceled, and may act accordingly to this. To avoid adding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new tasks